{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2358 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "f5525888d65e4eb1115e3719c66bea28c1bc6de155c5899ed3dcb09b698712fa" :edb/db-before-t 2357 :edb/db-after-t 2358 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535670 50 #inst "2026-10-09T04:47:19.099Z" 13194139535670 true] [17592186175860 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360271 13194139535670 true] [17592186175860 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360278 13194139535670 true] [17592186175861 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360250 13194139535670 true] [17592186175861 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360257 13194139535670 true] [17592186175861 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360264 13194139535670 true] [17592186360250 1017 #edb/ref 17592186360251 13194139535670 true] [17592186360250 1089 "q-149564" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360250 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535670 true] [17592186360250 1100 "| **Number of Members ($x$)** | $3$ | $4$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Number of Cars ($y$)** | $2$ | $2$ | $2$ | $6$ |\n\nIn a survey of $4$ families, the number of members in each family was recorded as well as the number of cars owned by that family. The data is shown in the table above.\nCompute the covariance of the data sets given that the means are $\\overset{―}{x}=4$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=3.$" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360250 1113 #uuid "308a128f-c3b5-54e4-a46d-fbae8dd63c97" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360250 1145 "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(3-4)(2-3)+(4-4)(2-3)+(4-4)(2-3)+(5-4)(6-3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-1)(-1)+(0)(-1)+(0)(-1)+(1)(3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[1+0+0+3] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360252 13194139535670 true] [17592186360251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360253 13194139535670 true] [17592186360251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360254 13194139535670 true] [17592186360251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360255 13194139535670 true] [17592186360251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360256 13194139535670 true] [17592186360251 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535670 true] [17592186360251 1041 "selection" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360251 1104 #edb/ref 17592186360255 13194139535670 true] [17592186360251 1110 #uuid "0e8303ce-a136-5edf-b143-3b65f3d1283c" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360252 1034 "2.5" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360252 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535670 true] [17592186360252 1111 #uuid "22e654fb-0cb3-564f-859e-684bc6ac3a2f" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360253 1034 "3" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360253 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535670 true] [17592186360253 1111 #uuid "9bd909b0-e213-5170-b17b-3edd5fa6d5f4" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360254 1034 "2" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360254 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535670 true] [17592186360254 1111 #uuid "bf82c987-3676-5344-9c1a-476ad9c51d48" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360255 1034 "1" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360255 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535670 true] [17592186360255 1111 #uuid "302061b9-bb5b-5632-8951-c1bcffce9658" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360256 1034 "-1" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360256 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535670 true] [17592186360256 1111 #uuid "eaab32b5-fb09-51f9-bb95-840e486945ac" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360257 1017 #edb/ref 17592186360258 13194139535670 true] [17592186360257 1089 "q-149570" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360257 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535670 true] [17592186360257 1100 "| **Years in the 1st division ($x$)** | $44$ | $38$ | $32$ | $30$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Number of Championships ($y$)** | $4$ | $3$ | $3$ | $6$ |\n\nThe table above shows the number of years four English soccer teams have been in the top division and the number of national championships they have won. \nCompute the covariance of the data sets." 13194139535670 true] [17592186360257 1113 #uuid "aedf8fc3-dbed-5730-9f21-b8c81e10ed3e" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360257 1145 "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (44+38+32+30) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 144 \\\\  & =36 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (4+3+3+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(44\\,-\\,36)(4\\,-\\,4)+(38\\,-\\,36)(3\\,-\\,4)+(32\\,-\\,36)(3\\,-\\,4)+(30\\,-\\,36)(6\\,-\\,4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(8)(0)+(2)(-1)+(-4)(-1)+(-6)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+(-2)+4+(-12)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-10) \\\\  & =-2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535670 true] [17592186360258 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360259 13194139535670 true] [17592186360258 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360260 13194139535670 true] [17592186360258 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360261 13194139535670 true] [17592186360258 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360262 13194139535670 true] [17592186360258 1000 #edb/ref 1